+// ---- gin-restore (rs): the restore request, strict window MRs, the setup agreement (EXPERIMENT.md 9.10.8) ----
+// A process asks for the restore when NCCL_GIN_FAULT_POLICY=hold and NCCL_GIN_RESTORE != 0 (default 1), or when it is a
+// spare process (NCCL_GIN_RESTORE_SPARE=<logical rank>). Such a process registers every GDAKI window MR with strict
+// ordering, whatever the application's window flags (ncclGinGdakiRegMrSym; user decision 2026-10-11). The registration
+// gets no error path of its own (one rank failing there would leave the others in the rkey all-gather). Instead every rank
+// carries "restore requested", "strict" and the facts that keep the restore off in its setup record (hk's policyPad), and
+// right after the setup all-gather every rank decides from the same records whether the restore can be enabled, and why
+// not (gdakiRsDecide). Under fail-fast (the default) none of this changes what hk does: no MR is forced, policyPad stays 0,
+// no line is added, the setup takes the same path. This build has no hold reaction yet: the effective policy stays
+// fail-fast (hk's G1), whatever the decision.
+NCCL_PARAM(GinRestore, "GIN_RESTORE", 1);       // gin-restore: 0 = no restore under hold (hold, never armed)
+extern int64_t ncclParamRMADisable();           // rma/rma.cc
+extern int64_t ncclParamSymGinKernelsEnable();  // sym_kernels.cc
